score_pct: 34.6
findings:
- finding_id: I1
  title: Dependencies inline instead of workspace level
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added uuid and chrono as workspace dependencies but the reviewer never
    flagged the 6 inline dependency versions. No phase addressed workspace-level dependency
    management comprehensively.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase mentioned #[non_exhaustive] on FieldErrorCode. The reviewer
    focused on other type issues but missed this enum extensibility concern.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: The reviewer noted hardcoded uptime '0s' but did not flag the hardcoded
    trace_id 'none' in ResponseMeta. No phase caught this distributed tracing gap.
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer explicitly noted in the data flow trace: ''No tracing spans.
    No structured logging. No tenant_id or trace_id in spans... there are zero tracing::
    calls anywhere in the implementation despite tracing being in Cargo.toml dependencies.''
    Also listed ''Add at least basic tracing::info! / tracing::warn! for auth events''
    as a recommendation.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: The reviewer identified the absence of logging but did not specifically
    flag misleading SECURITY comments claiming logging exists when it doesn't.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase wrote tests for non-ASCII tenant header values or flagged the
    silent failure behavior. TEA's authentication tests covered missing/invalid headers
    but not non-ASCII edge cases.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote a CWE-209 test but the reviewer did not flag that it only checks
    status code without asserting on response body content. The test gap went undetected.
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: Reviewer flagged '[MEDIUM] CORS reflects arbitrary Origin without allowlist'
    and noted 'The cors_does_not_allow_wildcard_origin_with_credentials test only
    checks the literal * value, not the actual reflection behavior.' This identifies
    the test doesn't verify actual CORS headers.
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: The reviewer recommended adding tracing but did not address log level
    granularity (warn for 4xx vs error for 5xx). Since no logging was implemented,
    the wrong-level issue couldn't manifest yet, but no phase established the correct
    pattern.
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[MEDIUM] CORS reflects arbitrary Origin without allowlist'\
    \ noting the handler 'echoes back whatever Origin header the client sends' which\
    \ is 'functionally Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * but worse \u2014 it works with\
    \ credentials.' Recommended 'CORS origin allowlist instead of reflection.'"
